<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52959" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάμηλος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, ὁ
		and ἡ (as in <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Av.</u>
			1563
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>camel, Camelus
				bactrianus</i> and <i>C. dromedarius</i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				499a13
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				285
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἔρσενας τῶν
			κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.105
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἀμνός</span>
			<i>a camel</i>-lamb, i.e. young camel, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1559
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δρομάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alex.</u>
					31
				</span></i>
			: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάμηλον καταπίνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
					23.24
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάμιλος</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κ</span>. <i>camelry</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.80
			</span></i>. (Semitic word, cf. Hebr.
			<i>gāmāl.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
